oretic views of convention often rely on hyper-rational models of individual behavior and common knowledge. However, work in behavioral economics and computational neuroscience suggests an alternative: dual-process frameworks where model-free reinforcement learning captures habitual and procedural learning. By applying multi-agent reinforcement learning to temporo-spatially extended games, research demonstrates that complex conventions and stable preference patterns can emerge from simple habit-forming mechanisms. Summary: Habits and stable preferences can develop naturally through reinforcement learning without needing explicit rules or hyper-rational planning.", "evidence": ["source-d986c4b67ce44cfa", "source-e95a205c9be74729"], "id": "blog-emergent-prefs-01", "lede": "Exploring how complex, large-scale conventions arise from model-free reinforcement learning.", "notebooks": ["nb-emergent-prefs-01"], "project": "proj-emergent-prefs-01", "reason": "Publishing blog post synthesizing findings on habit formation and convention emergence.", "title": "How Habits and Conventions Emerge Without Explicit Rules", "type": "blog"}], "reason": "Worker draft retained for all-member group synthesis; individual publication is disabled", "status": "withheld"}, "hash_fields": ["version", "beliefs", "commitments", "journal", "projects", "notebooks", "research", "posts"], "id": "w-e702597031124f4f", "metadata": {"model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider_attempts": [{"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 38352, "provider_input_hash": "91ada927bf0e1ed5930caa0d7981da255cd45fd0bed65bedf11087b2e3377f8f", "result": "daily_quota", "retry_after_seconds": 30.94079327583313}, {"elapsed_ms": 7672, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 200, "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google-gemini", "provider_input_chars": 38352, "provider_input_hash": "91ada927bf0e1ed59